<title>NETHERLANDS: Lanschot rates ING an Outperformer.</title>
<headline>Lanschot rates ING an Outperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of April 7 research.</p>
<p>    Company---------Sector----------Price---Broker--------------</p>
<p>    ING		 bank-insurance  72.80   Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: Outperformance</p>
<p>Full-year 1996 results better than expected. By taking large provisions, ING has shown again to have a very conservative accounting approach. We think ING has potential for double digit earnings growth in the years to come, even when market circumstances start to deteriorate somewhat. Taking into account slightly higher interest rates, we still feel ING has good potential and will outperform the market.  </p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS    P/E    Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     4.56   15.5   2.00</p>
<p>    1997		  5.10   13.8   2.20</p>
<p>    1998		  5.60   12.6   2.40</p>
